WEBVTT

00:00.310 --> 00:03.730
This is the last video in the course,
so well done for getting here.

00:05.080 --> 00:11.290
One question that comes up in my IELTS lessons
is how to fit everything into 20 minutes.

00:11.600 --> 00:16.600
You've learnt to read a graph, describe trends,
make comparisons and build a complete answer.

00:16.600 --> 00:19.450
Now you need to do it in 20 minutes.

00:20.790 --> 00:22.470
Here's how I'd split your time.

00:22.870 --> 00:23.970
Two minutes to plan.

00:24.430 --> 00:25.540
Fifteen minutes to write.

00:26.060 --> 00:27.240
And three minutes to check.

00:28.290 --> 00:32.300
Those last three minutes are protected.
Don't use them for writing.

00:32.300 --> 00:37.120
Use them to check your verbs, your tenses and your figures,
the things we've practised together.

00:38.270 --> 00:43.440
For your fifteen minutes of writing, aim for about
25 words in your introduction,

00:43.970 --> 00:48.770
30 in your overview and 50 to 60
in each body paragraph.

00:49.320 --> 00:52.800
That's over 150 words
without padding anything out.

00:53.800 --> 00:56.890
When you're ready, start the clock on the right page.

00:57.460 --> 00:58.600
Good luck.
